{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"title":"SegmentSpecEncoding","externalID":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records as Segment-spec track calls to Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segment, RudderStack and Customer.io Data Pipelines each take the same batch call of the Segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spec, at endpoints of their own. One encoder, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", writes it, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factory for each fills in the endpoint and how the key travels:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" posts to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the workspace’s region (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","type":"reference"},{"text":"), with the write key as HTTP Basic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authentication’s user name and an empty password.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":" posts to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/v1\/batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of your data plane URL, with the write key the same way.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" posts to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Pipelines API’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/v1\/batch"},{"type":"text","text":" in the workspace’s region ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), with the key as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bearer token and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X-Strict-Mode: 1"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each splits a batch to the spec’s limits (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":"): 2,500 calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and 500 KB a request, and under 32 KB a call, which all three accept. A batch with no record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. Each retries no response, a 5xx, 408","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The key goes in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization"},{"type":"text","text":" header field, never in the body. It is a public client key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment’s and RudderStack’s write keys, and Customer.io’s public keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pk_…"},{"type":"text","text":"), ship in their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vendors’ own app and web libraries, and they let a client send data to the source and read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s private keys ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sk_…"},{"type":"text","text":") reach every Customer.io API, deleting people included, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the factory throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError\/privateKey"},{"type":"text","text":" for one. Each factory throws for an empty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"},{"type":"text","text":"), RudderStack’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a data plane URL that isn’t a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL, and Customer.io’s for a public key of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other region."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A region has no default. Segment and Customer.io keep a workspace’s data in the US or the EU, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events posted to the other region’s endpoint don’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes a track call of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher; a record with no session is sent under its own record identifier. No","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call or traits are sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. The standard context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"goes in the spec’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" fields (","type":"text"},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"network","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"device.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"advertisingId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every call’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which Segment takes in place of the request’s address, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it records none. RudderStack fills in a ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the request unless the call has one,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"even beside ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and passes it on to its destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.0.0.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Customer.io’s references don’t say whether ","type":"text"},{"code":"context.ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes the place","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the address it reads from an HTTP request, so it may still record the request’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each endpoint counts a user per "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is each record sent without a session. On a plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. Segment deduplicates calls by "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops most duplicates within about 24 hours, not all, so one it stored before the app ended is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s API references don’t say whether"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they deduplicate, so such a record may be stored twice there."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one named as one of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices ("},{"code":"User Deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"User Suppressed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Device Deleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest), one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for a call. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination reports each as "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":", and the encoder logs a notice for each semantic event name in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan when the destination is made."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Segment answers 200 for every request but one too large or not JSON, so a wrong region, a write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key of no source, or a batch of more calls than it takes may be answered 200 with nothing stored."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Check the source’s debugger after setting the destination up. RudderStack answers a wrong write"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key with 401, and Customer.io, in strict mode, with 401 too, so the destination reports those. In"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"strict mode Customer.io refuses a whole batch for one bad call, so the encoder leaves out each call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io documents refusing; a 400 for anything else drops the whole request."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude or Mixpanel, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import SegmentSpecEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: segment)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what each endpoint receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Segment","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentRegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Segment"},{"title":"Sending to RudderStack","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/RudderStackSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-RudderStack"},{"title":"Sending to Customer.io Data Pipelines","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIORegion","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/CustomerIOSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Customerio-Data-Pipelines"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/docu